"k b"></span><span class="t">Shredding</span><svg class="c" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></div><div class="row"><span class="n">#61</span><span class="k b"></span><span class="t">Shredding</span><svg class="c" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></div><div class="row"><span class="n">#55</span><span class="k g"></span><span class="t">Dosing</span><svg class="c" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></div><div class="row"><span class="n">#52</span><span class="k g"></span><span class="t">Turbine</span><svg class="c" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></div></div><div class="cd"><div class="hd">Recommendations <i>view more <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></i></div><div class="row"><svg class="di" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><path d="M14 3v5h5"/></svg><span class="t">Shredding Maintenance</span><svg class="c" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></div><div class="row"><svg class="di" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><path d="M14 3v5h5"/></svg><span class="t">Detection of sparks</span><svg class="c" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></div><div class="row"><svg class="di" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><path d="M14 3v5h5"/></svg><span class="t">Training video</span><svg class="c" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></div></div></div><div class="toast"><span class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6"/></svg></span><div>Ticket #67 logged from the machine<small>QR scanned · Storing line · routed to OEM service desk</small></div></div><div class="fab"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 8V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v2M20 16v2a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-2M8 20H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-2"/><rect x="8" y="8" width="8" height="8" rx="1"/></svg></div></div></div><div class="ph b" aria-hidden="true"><span class="isl"></span><div class="scr"><div class="bar"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M4 12h16M4 17h16"/></svg><img class="lg" src="https://ithena.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ithena-Logo.webp" alt="ITHENA" width="568" height="188" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="sp"></span><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-3.5-3.5"/></svg><span class="av">JG</span></div><div class="body"><div class="tabs"><span>Tickets</span><span>Reports</span><span class="on">Knowledge Base</span></div><div class="pv">Swing Machine Repair</div><div class="vid"><span class="pl"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg></span></div><div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="dl pdf"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><path d="M14 3v5h5"/></svg><span class="sp">Machine Maintenance Training</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v12M6 12l6 6 6-6M4 20h16"/></svg></div><div class="dl xls"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><path d="M14 3v5h5"/></svg><span class="sp">Maintenance Spread Sheets</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v12M6 12l6 6 6-6M4 20h16"/></svg></div><div class="pv">Preview the PDF</div><div class="pdfbox">1. Push Start button<div class="note">NOTE: make sure all other equipment at the ITHENA line is turned ON.</div><div class="ln m"></div><div class="ln s"></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="rv"><div class="head" style="margin-bottom:0"><p class="eb">In their pocket</p><h2>And the App Your Customer <span class="grad">Never Puts Down.</span></h2><p class="lede">The dashboards above are for the desk. This is for the person standing at the machine: they scan its QR code, log the ticket with the photo, and open the right manual or how-to video on the spot, while your service desk sees it the moment it lands. Self-servicing at your fingertips, on iOS and Android.</p></div><div class="pil"><div class="pi"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 14v-2a8 8 0 0 1 16 0v2"/><path d="M4 14a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h1v6H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2zM20 14a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-1v6h1a2 2 0 0 0 2-2z"/><path d="M17 18a3 3 0 0 1-3 3h-2"/></svg></span><div><h3>Service Support</h3><ul><li><b>Self-guided content:</b> Access comprehensive tutorials, FAQs, and how-to guides for independent troubleshooting and maintenance</li><li><b>Integrated ticketing &amp; case management:</b> Log, prioritize, and track service requests with real-time updates and transparent communication</li><li><b>Remote collaboration with AR/VR:</b> Utilize AR/VR technologies for real-time, virtual assistance and guidance, reducing downtime and enhancing efficiency</li></ul></div></div><div class="pi"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h13v16H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2z"/><path d="M4 19a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h13"/><path d="M8 7h7"/></svg></span><div><h3>Knowledge Portal</h3><ul><li><b>Knowledge artifacts for self-service:</b> Troubleshooting guides and FAQs for independent issue resolution</li><li><b>Content hub with document management:</b> Centralized repository for manuals and technical documents, ensuring easy access and updates</li><li><b>How-to videos &amp; machine schematics:</b> Visual guides and diagrams for understanding equipment operation and maintenance</li></ul></div></div><div class="pi"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="3" width="14" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M9 8h6M9 12h6M9 16h3"/></svg></span><div><h3>Service Operation</h3><ul><li><b>Customer onboarding:</b> Comprehensive training and support for smooth integration of our services</li><li><b>Technician scheduling &amp; routing:</b> Optimize technician deployment with real-time data and intelligent algorithms for efficient service</li><li><b>Enhanced service experience:</b> Proactive communication, real-time updates, and personalized interactions for exceptional customer satisfaction</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></section>
<!--/ithena-mobile-app-->
<section class="sec" id="aether"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head rv"><p class="eb">Aether AI Platform</p>
    <h2>Ask the Installed Base <span class="grad">a Question.</span></h2>
    <p class="lede">Aether sits on top of iSERV. Put a question to it in your own words and it comes back with the finding, the visual behind it, and the button that acts on&nbsp;it.</p></div>
  <div class="agrid">
    <div class="asticky"><div class="rv panel"><div class="glass"><div class="ui ">
  <div class="ui-top"><span class="ui-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
    <span class="ui-url">iserv.ithena.ai / aether</span><span class="ui-av">JG</span></div>
  <div class="ui-chat">
  <div class="ui-q"><span class="who">You</span>Which assets lost the most hours to unplanned stops last quarter?</div>
  <div class="ui-a"><span class="who ai">Aether</span>
    <p>Four assets account for 78% of unplanned downtime. Line 3 leads on glue-missing stops.</p>
    <div class="ui-mini"><div class="mb"><i style="--h:44%"></i><i style="--h:68%"></i><i style="--h:52%"></i><i style="--h:88%"></i><i style="--h:60%"></i><i style="--h:74%"></i><i style="--h:96%"></i></div>
      <p class="cap">Unplanned downtime by asset · last quarter</p></div>
    <div class="ui-act"><i>Raise 4 work orders</i><i class="g">Order the seal kits</i></div>
  </div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div>
    <div class="afeat"><article class="rv" style="--d:0.00s"><span class="ic"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.9 20A9 9 0 1 0 4 16.1L2 22Z"/></svg></span><h3>NLP-Driven Chat</h3><p>Ask about a machine, a ticket or a component in plain language and get the answer back.</p></article><article class="rv" style="--d:0.06s"><span class="ic"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v1a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7v1a4 4 0 0 1-8 0v-1a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0-7V7a4 4 0 0 1 4-4z"/><path d="M12 8v8M9.5 11h5"/></svg></span><h3>GenAI-Powered Insights</h3><p>Summarised findings across service history rather than raw rows to read.</p></article><article class="rv" style="--d:0.12s"><span class="ic"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 12s3.6-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3.6 7-10 7-10-7-10-7z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg></span><h3>Real-Time Visualization</h3><p>The answer comes back as a chart of current data, not a static export.</p></article><article class="rv" style="--d:0.18s"><span class="ic"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="1.4"/><rect x="14" y="14" width="7" height="7" rx="1.4"/><path d="M10 6.5h3.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 16 9v5"/><path d="m13.6 12.2 2.4 2.3 2.4-2.3"/></svg></span><h3>Multi-Source Data Integration</h3><p>Equipment telemetry, case history and commerce, answered in one place.</p></article><article class="rv" style="--d:0.24s"><span class="ic"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg></span><h3>Enterprise-Scale Intelligence</h3><p>Built for whole installed bases, with role-based access to what each user may see.</p></article><article class="rv" style="--d:0.30s"><span class="ic"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 2 3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z"/></svg></span><h3>Agentic Actions</h3><p>It can raise the case or start the order it just recommended.</p></article></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="proofwrap" id="proof"><div class="dk dkblock"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head rv"><p class="eb">Success stories</p>
    <h2>Discover iSERV <span class="grad">Success Stories.</span></h2>
    <p class="lede">Two deployments, two very different machines, and the same starting point: no live view of equipment once it left the factory.</p></div>
  <div class="cases">
    <article class="case rv">
      <p class="tg"><span>Metal forming and forging</span><span>Predictive maintenance</span></p>
      <h3>Deploying ITHENA’s iSERV to Enhance Operations at the Leading Metal-forming and Forging Company</h3>
      <p>The client, a frontrunner in the metal forging sector, aimed to embrace data-driven manufacturing to enhance plant efficiency. Implementing iSERV in their machinery facilitated real-time access to critical equipment parameters via personalised dashboards, empowering users to conduct predictive maintenance activities. Additionally, iSERV enabled users to access a knowledge repository and provided self-help videos and manuals for enhanced operational effectiveness.</p>
      <p class="met"><b data-count="18" data-suffix="%">18%</b><span>enhanced efficiency</span></p>
      <a class="rd" href="https://ithena.ai/case-studies/">Read the case study<svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
    </article>
    <article class="case rv" style="--d:.1s">
      <p class="tg"><span>Sampling and analysis</span><span>Smart service application</span></p>
      <h3>iSERV, ITHENA’s Smart Service Application for the World’s Leading Sampling Expert</h3>
      <p>Our client offers sampling and analysis techniques to customers around the globe that enables them to increase production efficiency and output. The client was facing frequent breakdown in machines that required easy information manual for the customers. Also, there was no unified platform to raise queries and concerns to get a quick resolution. ITHENA’s smart service application, iSERV, monitored the performance of equipment and enabled predictive maintenance for the customer. With iSERV, the client is able to quickly identify performance issues before downtime.</p>
      <p class="met"><b data-count="38" data-suffix="%">38%</b><span>customer satisfaction</span></p>
      <a class="rd" href="https://ithena.ai/case-studies/">Read the case study<svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="allcase rv"><a href="https://ithena.ai/case-studies/">See every ITHENA case study<svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></a></p>
</div></div></section>
</main>

<section class="final">
  <div class="fin">
    <p class="eb rv">Get started</p>
    <h2 class="rv">Ready to <span class="grad">Elevate OEM Profits</span>?</h2>
    <p class="lede rv">Bring your own machines and a month of tickets. We will show you what iSERV does with them, in a working session rather than a slideshow.</p>
    <div class="btns rv"><a class="btn pri" href="/contact-us/">Schedule Demo<span class="arw"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></a><a class="btn ghost" href="/contact-us/">Talk to the team<span class="arw"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="fmw" id="fmw" hidden><div class="fmveil" data-fmclose></div><div class="fmpanel" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="fmtitle"><button class="fmx" type="button" data-fmclose aria-label="Close this form"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg></button><div class="fmhead"><p class="eb">Talk to us</p><h2 id="fmtitle">Book Your iSERV Walkthrough.</h2><p class="fmlede">Tell us what you build and who looks after it in the field, and we will come back with a time that suits your team.</p></div><div class="fmbody">[formidable id=44]</div></div></div>
</div>
<script>
(function () {
  var reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  /* reveal — also the trigger that draws every gauge, bar and line inside a console */
  var els = [].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.rv'));
  if ('IntersectionObserver' in window && !reduce) {
    var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (es) {
      es.forEach(function (e) {
        if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(e.target); }
      });
    }, { rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px', threshold: .12 });
    els.forEach(function (e) { io.observe(e); });
  } else {
    els.forEach(function (e) { e.classList.add('in'); });
  }

  /* count up the outcome numbers */
  function countUp(el) {
    var t = parseFloat(el.dataset.count), s = el.dataset.suffix || '', st = null;
    function step(ts) {
      if (!st) st = ts;
      var p = Math.min((ts - st) / 1100, 1); p = 1 - Math.pow(1 - p, 3);
      el.textContent = Math.round(t * p) + s;
      if (p < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);
    }
    requestAnimationFrame(step);
  }
  var mets = document.querySelectorAll('[data-count]');
  if (mets.length && 'IntersectionObserver' in window && !reduce) {
    var mo = new IntersectionObserver(function (es) {
      es.forEach(function (e) { if (e.isIntersecting) { countUp(e.target); mo.unobserve(e.target); } });
    }, { threshold: .6 });
    mets.forEach(function (m) { mo.observe(m); });
  }

  /* console tabs. Panels keep their charts undrawn until shown, so switching a tab
     replays that screen's animation instead of revealing a finished still. */
  var tabs = [].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.tabs [role="tab"]'));
  tabs.forEach(function (tab) {
    tab.addEventListener('click', function () {
      tabs.forEach(function (t) {
        var pane = document.getElementById(t.getAttribute('aria-controls'));
        var on = t === tab;
        t.setAttribute('aria-selected', on ? 'true' : 'false');
        if (!pane) return;
        pane.classList.toggle('on', on);
        if (on) { pane.classList.remove('in'); void pane.offsetWidth; pane.classList.add('in'); }
      });
    });
    tab.addEventListener('keydown', function (ev) {
      var i = tabs.indexOf(tab), n = null;
      if (ev.key === 'ArrowRight') n = tabs[(i + 1) % tabs.length];
      if (ev.key === 'ArrowLeft') n = tabs[(i - 1 + tabs.length) % tabs.length];
      if (n) { ev.preventDefault(); n.focus(); n.click(); }
    });
  });

  /* card stack: as the next card rides up over this one, scale this one back a little
     (--p, 0..1) so the pile reads as depth rather than a hard cut */
  var cards = [].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.pstack .dcard'));
  if (cards.length > 1 && !reduce) {
    var ticking = false;
    function stack() {
      ticking = false;
      for (var i = 0; i < cards.length - 1; i++) {
        var a = cards[i].getBoundingClientRect(), b = cards[i + 1].getBoundingClientRect();
        var p = (a.bottom - b.top) / a.height;
        cards[i].style.setProperty('--p', Math.max(0, Math.min(1, p)).toFixed(3));
      }
    }
    addEventListener('scroll', function () { if (!ticking) { ticking = true; requestAnimationFrame(stack); } }, { passive: true });
    stack();
  }

  /* pointer parallax on the hero console */
  var stage = document.querySelector('.hstage');
  if (stage && !reduce && matchMedia('(hover:hover)').matches) {
    var ui = stage.querySelector('.ui');
    stage.addEventListener('mousemove', function (e) {
      var r = stage.getBoundingClientRect();
      var x = (e.clientX - r.left) / r.width - .5, y = (e.clientY - r.top) / r.height - .5;
      ui.style.transform = 'rotateY(' + (-4 + x * 5).toFixed(2) + 'deg) rotateX(' + (-y * 3).toFixed(2) + 'deg)';
    });
    stage.addEventListener('mouseleave', function () { ui.style.transform = ''; });
  }
})();

/* ---- CTA form modal -------------------------------------------------------
   Every CTA is a real link to /contact-us/; this intercepts the click. One
   delegated listener on the document means CTAs added later are wired for free. */
(function () {
  var w = document.getElementById('fmw');
  if (!w) return;
  var panel = w.querySelector('.fmpanel'), last = null;

  /* position:fixed is relative to the nearest transformed ancestor, and this markup
     is pasted into a container we do not own. Re-parent to <body> and the question
     stops being askable. The host keeps the page scope class for the tokens and the
     font; the background and clipping that class also carries are neutralised. */
  var host = document.createElement('div');
  host.className = 'is';
  host.style.cssText = 'background:none;overflow:visible;color:inherit';
  host.appendChild(w);
  document.body.appendChild(host);

  function focusables() {
    return [].slice.call(panel.querySelectorAll(
      'a[href],button:not([disabled]),input:not([type=hidden]):not([disabled]),textarea,select,[tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])'
    )).filter(function (el) { return el.offsetParent !== null || el === document.activeElement; });
  }

  function open(trigger) {
    if (w.classList.contains('on')) return;
    last = trigger || document.activeElement;
    w.hidden = false;
    w.classList.add('on');
    document.documentElement.style.overflow = 'hidden';
    /* Focus moves now, not inside the animation frame. An element at opacity 0 is still
       focusable, and requestAnimationFrame is not guaranteed to run promptly — under a
       throttled or background frame clock it can be skipped entirely, which left the
       dialog open with focus still on the body. Only the transition class waits. */
    var field = panel.querySelector('input:not([type=hidden]),textarea,select');
    (field || focusables()[0] || panel).focus({ preventScroll: true });
    requestAnimationFrame(function () { w.classList.add('in'); });
  }

  function close() {
    if (!w.classList.contains('on')) return;
    w.classList.remove('in');
    document.documentElement.style.overflow = '';
    var done = function () { w.classList.remove('on'); w.hidden = true; };
    if (matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce)').matches) done();
    else setTimeout(done, 300);
    if (last && last.focus) last.focus({ preventScroll: true });
  }

  document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    var cta = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('a[href="/contact-us/"]');
    if (cta) { e.preventDefault(); open(cta); return; }
    if (e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-fmclose]')) { e.preventDefault(); close(); }
  });

  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
    if (!w.classList.contains('on')) return;
    if (e.key === 'Escape') { close(); return; }
    if (e.key !== 'Tab') return;
    var f = focusables();
    if (!f.length) return;
    var first = f[0], lastEl = f[f.length - 1];
    if (e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) { e.preventDefault(); lastEl.focus(); }
    else if (!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === lastEl) { e.preventDefault(); first.focus(); }
  });

  /* Form 122 posts the whole page rather than submitting over AJAX, so the reply comes
     back with the confirmation or the validation errors rendered inside a modal that is
     closed. Re-open it when that is what happened. Harmless if AJAX submit is enabled
     later: the branch is simply never taken. */
  if (w.querySelector('.frm_message, .frm_error_style, .frm_blank_field')) open(null);
})();

</script>
<style id="ithena-ads-page-patch">
/* --- ITHENA ads-page patch (iSERV) ------------------------------------------
   Scoped by body.page-id so the global Elementor header (65338) and
   footer (98) templates are untouched everywhere else on the site. */

/* 1. Elementor's column wrapper ships padding:10px; body is #181818, so the
      dark background reads as a border on all four sides of the page. */
body.page-id-51344 .elementor-51344 .elementor-widget-wrap.elementor-element-populated{
  padding:0 !important;
}

/* 2. The header is run by the Sticky Header Effects plugin with
      transparent:yes / background:#181818, i.e. see-through at the top of the
      page and only filling in on scroll - so the white logo + nav vanish over
      a light hero. The plugin rewrites background-color inline at runtime, so
      setting that property is fragile. Paint the bar with a pseudo-element
      underneath the header content instead - the plugin never touches it.
      #181818 is the exact colour the plugin itself uses once scrolled, so the
      static bar and the scrolled bar are identical (no colour jump). */
body.page-id-51344 header.elementor-location-header > section.elementor-top-section{
  position:relative;
  /* The section is 80px but its nav row is only 70px - a 10px padding-bottom left
     a strip of black hanging under the nav, so the bar sat taller than the compact
     one the rest of the site shows once scrolled. Close the gap. */
  padding-bottom:0 !important;
}
body.page-id-51344 header.elementor-location-header > section.elementor-top-section::before{
  content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:0;pointer-events:none;
  background:#181818;
}
body.page-id-51344 header.elementor-location-header > section.elementor-top-section > *{
  position:relative;z-index:1;
}

/* 3. section.final ships border-radius:0 0 40px 40px - it was drawn to read as a
      floating card back when the 10px inset (fix 1) framed it. Full-bleed those
      curves just look like a mistake against the footer, so square them off.
      NOTE: no gradient here on purpose. An earlier version of this patch faded
      the section into the footer and it greyed out the CTA - the section's own
      styling is what should show. */
body.page-id-51344 section.final{border-radius:0 !important}

/* 4. CTA popup - force it light. The shared modal was built dark (it inherited the
      site's dark .frm_forms styling); asked for a white, clean panel. Scoped to the
      modal classes only, so no other Formidable form on the site is touched.
      This block sits at the END of the page markup, so at equal specificity it wins
      the cascade over the page's own earlier <style>. */
.fmveil{background:rgba(13,27,46,.55) !important;backdrop-filter:blur(4px)}
.fmpanel{
  background:#FFFFFF !important;color:#1F2023 !important;
  border:1px solid #EAEAEA !important;border-radius:16px !important;
  box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(13,27,46,.22) !important;
}
.fmpanel .fmhead h2{color:#1F2023 !important}
.fmpanel .fmlede{color:rgba(0,0,0,.66) !important}
.fmpanel .fmhead .eb,.fmpanel .fmhead .kicker{color:#0083C8 !important}
/* Close button: iSERV's own rule left the glyph sitting low and right of centre.
   Grid centring plus a zeroed line-box pins it dead centre on both pages. */
.fmpanel .fmx{
  color:#1F2023 !important;background:#F4F4F4 !important;
  border:1px solid #EAEAEA !important;border-radius:50% !important;
  width:36px !important;height:36px !important;padding:0 !important;
  display:grid !important;place-items:center !important;
  line-height:0 !important;font-size:0 !important;
}
.fmpanel .fmx svg{
  width:16px !important;height:16px !important;display:block !important;margin:0 !important;
}
.fmpanel .fmx:hover{background:#EAEAEA !important}

/* The form itself is painted by the SITE-WIDE Formidable theme
   (.frm_forms.with_frm_style.frm_style_formidable-style), which is dark:
   fieldset #191919, .frm_fields_container #0F1216, inputs #0F1216 on #F3F5F7 text,
   labels #8D959F. Selectors below match that specificity so the panel reads light.
   Everything is under .fmbody, so no other Formidable form on the site changes. */
.fmbody .frm_forms,
.fmbody .with_frm_style,
.fmbody .with_frm_style form,
.fmbody .with_frm_style fieldset,
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_form_fields,
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_fields_container,
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_form_field{
  background:transparent !important;color:#1F2023 !important;
  border:0 !important;box-shadow:none !important;padding:0 !important;
}
.fmbody .with_frm_style label,
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_primary_label{
  color:#1F2023 !important;font-weight:600 !important;text-transform:none !important;
  letter-spacing:normal !important;font-size:13px !important;
}
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_required{color:#D9534F !important}
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_description{color:#797979 !important}
.fmbody .with_frm_style input:not([type=submit]):not([type=button]):not([type=checkbox]):not([type=radio]),
.fmbody .with_frm_style textarea,
.fmbody .with_frm_style select{
  background:#FFFFFF !important;color:#1F2023 !important;
  border:1px solid #D9DDE2 !important;border-radius:10px !important;
  box-shadow:none !important;height:auto !important;padding:11px 13px !important;
}
.fmbody .with_frm_style input:not([type=submit]):focus,
.fmbody .with_frm_style textarea:focus,
.fmbody .with_frm_style select:focus{
  border-color:#0083C8 !important;outline:none !important;
  box-shadow:0 0 0 3px rgba(0,131,200,.16) !important;
}
.fmbody .with_frm_style input::placeholder,
.fmbody .with_frm_style textarea::placeholder{color:#A2A2A2 !important}
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_submit{margin:16px 0 0 !important}
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_button_submit,
.fmbody .with_frm_style input[type=submit],
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_submit>button{
  background:#0083C8 !important;color:#FFFFFF !important;border:0 !important;
  border-radius:999px !important;font-weight:700 !important;
  padding:13px 26px !important;width:auto !important;cursor:pointer !important;
}
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_button_submit:hover,
.fmbody .with_frm_style input[type=submit]:hover{background:#006AA3 !important}
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_error{color:#D9534F !important}
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_error_style{
  color:#8A2B28 !important;background:#FDECEC !important;border:1px solid #F3C4C3 !important}
.fmbody .with_frm_style .frm_message{
  color:#12674A !important;background:#E8F7F0 !important;border:1px solid #B7E5D2 !important}
</style>
<!-- ithena-font-pass -->
<style>
/* Font pass (2026-08-27, user instruction) - FONT ONLY, nothing else.
   Headings: Noto Sans 800 (site heading font).  Body copy / liners: Arial (site body font).
   Written with the .is scope; ads/font_pass.py swaps it to .mx for the PanelOps pages.
   Mock product screens (.ui-*), phones (.ph), stat numerals and the flow-map labels are
   artwork rather than copy, so they keep Noto Sans. */
.is{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}
.is h1,.is h2,.is h3,.is h4,.is h5,.is h6{font-family:"Noto Sans",-apple-system,"system-ui","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif!important}
.is h1,.is h2{font-weight:800!important}
.is .ui,.is [class^="ui-"],.is [class*=" ui-"],.is .ph,.is .nums b,.is .hfloat b,.is .met b,.is .fm text{font-family:"Noto Sans",-apple-system,"system-ui","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif}
</style>
<!-- /ithena-font-pass -->
<!-- ithena-iserv-restructure -->
<style>
/* iSERV page restructure, 2026-08-28 (v2).
   Three additions, all reusing the page's own tokens, .wrap, .tags, .head, .rv, .panel
   and the hand-drawn consoles: the three merged module cards in one row (.ibsec), and
   the #console tabs rebuilt as the CRM reference's sticky stage stack (.stx-*).
   Every position lives in a class, never in a style attribute: an inline offset
   outranks every media query below and cannot be pulled back in on a phone. */

/* ---- the three merged modules, one row ------------------------------------- */
.is .ibsec{padding:clamp(48px,5.6vw,84px) 0 clamp(30px,3.4vw,52px);background:var(--bg)}
.is .ibrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:clamp(14px,1.8vw,26px)}
.is .ibcard{display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius:var(--r3);padding:clamp(14px,1.6vw,22px);
  transition:transform .45s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1),box-shadow .45s,border-color .45s}
.is .ibcard:hover{transform:translateY(-6px);border-color:#CFE0EC;
  box-shadow:0 34px 64px -34px rgba(0,40,70,.45)}
/* the supplied illustrations are square with transparent corners; a fixed-ratio frame
   keeps the three the same height however each was cropped */
.is .ibfig{margin:0 0 clamp(14px,1.6vw,20px);aspect-ratio:1/1;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--r2);
  background:linear-gradient(180deg,#F4F8FB,#EAF3F9);display:grid;place-items:center;padding:6%}
.is .ibfig img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain;
  transition:transform .7s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
.is .ibcard:hover .ibfig img{transform:scale(1.05)}
.is .ibno{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-bottom:10px}
.is .ibno b{font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--ink-4)}
.is .ibno .ic{width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:8px;display:grid;place-items:center;
  flex:none;background:var(--wash);color:var(--blue);transition:background-color .3s,color .3s}
.is .ibno .ic .i{width:16px;height:16px}
.is .ibcard:hover .ibno .ic{background:var(--blue);color:#fff}
/* three columns cannot hold these titles on one line; hold two lines for every card
   instead, so the copy below starts at the same height across the row */
.is .ibcard h3{font-size:clamp(17px,1.35vw,20px);letter-spacing:-.012em;line-height:1.25;
  margin:0 0 8px;min-height:2.5em;color:var(--ink)}
.is .ibcard>p{font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0}
.is .ibcard .tags{margin-top:auto;padding-top:14px}
/* each card is a link to the section that shows the module at work (CEO, 2026-08-28) */
.is a.ibcard{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}
.is .iblink{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin-top:14px;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;
  color:var(--blue);letter-spacing:-.005em}
.is .iblink .i{width:15px;height:15px;transition:transform .35s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
.is .ibcard:hover .iblink .i{transform:translateX(4px)}
/* the fixed site header is 70px: the linked sections land with the heading in view */
.is #loop,.is #mobile,.is #console,.is #who{scroll-margin-top:84px}
/* customer-view service desk: ticket list and next-visit block */
.is .stx-dkrow{grid-template-columns:1.55fr 1fr}
.is .stx-tk{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.5fr .9fr .9fr .9fr;gap:6px;align-items:center;
  font-size:10px;color:#3D4E5C;padding:7px 0;border-top:1px solid #EEF2F6}
.is .stx-tk.hd{border-top:0;padding-top:0;font-size:8.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.05em;
  text-transform:uppercase;color:#8494A2}
.is .stx-tk .m{line-height:1.25}
.is .stx-tk .m b{display:block;font-size:11px;color:#16222E}
.is .stx-tk .st{display:inline-block;justify-self:start;font-size:9px;font-weight:700;border-radius:100px;padding:3px 8px}
.is .stx-tk .st.b{background:#E3F2FC;color:#0069A5}
.is .stx-tk .st.a{background:#FDF0DC;color:#B26F0E}
.is .stx-tk .st.g{background:#E1F5EC;color:#1B7F55}
.is .stx-dkap{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;margin-top:2px;padding:9px 10px;border-radius:9px;
  background:#F4F7FA;font-size:10px;color:#54636F}
.is .stx-dkap b{font-size:13px;color:#16222E}

/* ---- console as a sticky stage stack ------------------------------------------ */
/* the pill rail pins under the site header; the panels pin lower, clear of the rail */
.is .stx-rail{position:relative;z-index:30;display:flex;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:30px}
.is .stx-rail>*{min-width:0;max-width:100%}
.is .stx-rail{flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:8px}
.is .stx-sb{display:none;position:relative;flex:0 0 100%;height:4px;margin:0 16px;border-radius:4px;background:rgba(0,131,200,.14)}
.is .stx-sb.on{display:block}
.is .stx-sb i{position:absolute;top:0;bottom:0;left:0;width:40%;border-radius:4px;background:var(--blue);transition:left .12s linear}
.is .stx-pills{display:inline-flex;gap:4px;padding:6px;border-radius:100px;
  background:rgba(250,250,250,.78);backdrop-filter:blur(22px) saturate(180%);
  border:1px solid var(--line);box-shadow:0 18px 40px -22px rgba(0,40,70,.35);
  max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none}
.is .stx-pills::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
.is .stx-pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex:none;font:inherit;
  padding:8px 20px 8px 8px;border-radius:100px;border:1px solid transparent;background:transparent;
  cursor:pointer;color:var(--ink-2);font-size:14.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;
  transition:color .3s,background-color .3s,box-shadow .3s}
.is .stx-pill i{width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;flex:none;
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pc) 15%,transparent);color:var(--pc);
  transition:background-color .3s,color .3s,transform .35s}
.is .stx-pill i svg{width:16px;height:16px}
.is .stx-pill:hover{color:var(--ink);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pc) 8%,transparent)}
.is .stx-pill.on{color:#fff;background:var(--pc);
  box-shadow:0 12px 26px -12px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pc) 95%,transparent)}
.is .stx-pill.on i{background:#fff;color:var(--pc);transform:scale(1.08)}
/* spacing between stages is a SPACER SIBLING, never a margin on the panel: a sticky box
   is released by its own margin box, so a margin would unpin every card early */
.is .stx{position:relative}
/* one card at a time; the panels share one grid cell, the active one pops from the centre */
.is .stx-panels{display:grid;padding-bottom:0}
.is .stx-panel{position:static;top:auto;grid-area:1/1;align-self:start;opacity:0;visibility:hidden;pointer-events:none}
.is .stx-panel.on{opacity:1;visibility:visible;pointer-events:auto}
.is .stx-panel.in{animation:stxin .28s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1) both}
@keyframes stxin{from{opacity:0;transform:scale(.9)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}
.is .stx-card{position:relative;border-radius:var(--r3);overflow:hidden;background:var(--white);
  border:1px solid var(--line);
  box-shadow:0 30px 70px -40px rgba(0,40,70,.35),0 40px 90px -50px color-mix(in srgb,var(--ac) 85%,transparent);
  display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.8fr) minmax(0,1.2fr)}
.is .stx-copy{position:relative;padding:clamp(28px,3.2vw,46px) clamp(22px,2.8vw,40px);
  display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;overflow:hidden}
.is .stx-ghost{position:absolute;top:-22px;right:16px;z-index:0;pointer-events:none;user-select:none;
  font-size:clamp(110px,11vw,170px);font-weight:800;line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.06em;
  color:var(--ac);opacity:.07}
.is .stx-copy>*:not(.stx-ghost){position:relative;z-index:1}
.is .stx-num{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;align-self:flex-start;margin:0 0 16px;
  padding:6px 14px 6px 8px;border-radius:100px;
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ac) 12%,transparent);
  border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--ac) 26%,transparent);
  font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ac)}
.is .stx-num b{width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;
  background:linear-gradient(140deg,var(--ac),var(--ac2));color:#fff;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0}
.is .stx-copy h3{font-size:clamp(22px,2.3vw,32px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--ink)}
.is .stx-lede{font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin:0}
.is .stx-facts{list-style:none;margin:20px 0 0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px}
.is .stx-facts li{position:relative;padding-left:27px;font-size:13.8px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5}
.is .stx-facts li::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:3px;width:17px;height:17px;border-radius:50%;
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ac) 15%,transparent)}
.is .stx-facts li::after{content:"";position:absolute;left:5px;top:8px;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;
  background:linear-gradient(140deg,var(--ac),var(--ac2))}
.is .stx-tag{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;align-self:flex-start;margin-top:24px;
  padding:8px 16px;border-radius:100px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;background:var(--navy);color:#fff}
.is .stx-tag .dot{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ac2);flex:none}
/* the visual half: the page's own console on the stage's colour */
.is .stx-vis{position:relative;overflow:hidden;padding:clamp(20px,2.6vw,40px);
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  background:radial-gradient(78% 66% at 14% 8%,color-mix(in srgb,var(--ac2) 78%,transparent),transparent 68%),
    radial-gradient(72% 78% at 96% 92%,color-mix(in srgb,var(--ac) 92%,transparent),transparent 70%),
    linear-gradient(146deg,var(--ac) 0%,var(--ac2) 58%,var(--ac) 100%)}
.is .stx-vis::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;opacity:.16;
  background-image:linear-gradient(to right,#fff 1px,transparent 1px),linear-gradient(to bottom,#fff 1px,transparent 1px);
  background-size:40px 40px;-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(215deg,#000,transparent 66%);
  mask-image:linear-gradient(215deg,#000,transparent 66%)}
.is .stx-vis>.panel{position:relative;width:100%;background:transparent;padding:0;border-radius:0;overflow:visible}
.is .stx-vis>.panel::before{display:none}
.is .stx-vis .glass{width:100%}
/* a real product screen instead of the hand-drawn console (2026-09-03). width:100% with
   height:auto is the whole guarantee: the drawings carried their own intrinsic size and
   .stx-vis's overflow:hidden cut the last row off every table. .shot drops the padding a
   little so the screen reads at a usable size inside the same gradient. */
.is .stx-shot{margin:0;width:100%;max-width:100%}
.is .stx-shot img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:14px;background:#fff;
  border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.55);
  box-shadow:0 26px 60px -26px rgba(0,26,48,.55),0 6px 18px -8px rgba(0,26,48,.35)}
.is .stx-vis.shot{padding:clamp(16px,2vw,30px)}
/* switching stages must be a cut, not a cross-fade (user, 2026-09-03: "the screen of
   previous gets stuck and then changes to new"). .stx-vis also carries .rv, and .rv's own
   0.7s opacity+translate reveal ran again every time a stage was opened, so the new screen
   arrived a beat late and the old one looked like it hung. The panel's .28s scale-in is the
   only entrance this needs; the class stays because the console gauges key off .rv.in. */
.is .stx-panel .stx-vis.rv{opacity:1;transform:none;transition:none}
.is .stx-chip{position:absolute;z-index:3;right:clamp(10px,1.4vw,22px);bottom:clamp(10px,1.4vw,22px);
  display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius:12px;padding:9px 13px;box-shadow:0 22px 46px -20px rgba(0,40,70,.45)}
.is .stx-chip .k{display:block;font-size:9.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-4)}
.is .stx-chip .v{display:block;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);margin-top:2px;white-space:nowrap}

/* ---- v3 (CEO list, 2026-08-28) ------------------------------------------------ */
/* hero: the site header is a transparent overlay (she-header), so the page starts at
   y=0 underneath it - 70px tall on desktop, 64px on tablet/phone. The eyebrow sat
   28px under it on desktop and behind it on phones. The h1's coloured span was nowrap,
   which the longer "Aftermarket Service Platform" cannot afford on a phone */
.is .hero{padding-top:clamp(110px,8vw,122px)}
.is .hero h1 .grad{white-space:normal}
/* the desktop mega-menu drops ~8px below the header and the hero showed through that
   strip; a band in the header colour under the header (80px) makes the strip read as
   header. z:1 keeps it under .wrap, whose content starts at 110px */
@media (min-width:1025px){
  .is .hero::before{content:"";position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;height:80px;background:#181818;z-index:1}
}
/* v4 capability cards (mockup, 2026-08-28 evening): full-bleed 4:3 photo on top with a
   round badge overlapping its bottom-left corner, number / title / copy, a two-column
   feature list with a glyph per row, and a full-width button as the card's cue line */
.is .ibrow{gap:clamp(12px,1.5vw,22px)}
.is .ibcard{padding:0;overflow:hidden;border-radius:18px;container-type:inline-size}
.is .ibfig{position:relative;margin:0;aspect-ratio:4/3;border-radius:0;padding:0;background:#E9F1F8;display:block;overflow:visible}
.is .ibfig img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;border-radius:18px 18px 0 0}
.is .ibcard:hover .ibfig img{transform:none}
.is .ibbadge{position:absolute;left:22px;bottom:-27px;z-index:2;width:54px;height:54px;border-radius:50%;
  background:var(--blue);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;border:3px solid #fff;
  box-shadow:0 8px 20px -8px rgba(0,60,110,.5)}
.is .ibbadge .i{width:24px;height:24px}
.is .ibbody{display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;padding:38px 22px 22px}
.is .ibno{margin-bottom:6px}
.is .ibno b{color:var(--blue);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em}
.is .ibcard h3{font-size:clamp(18px,1.4vw,22px);min-height:0;margin:0 0 10px}
.is .ibbody>p{font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 14px;min-height:0}
.is .ibfeat{list-style:none;margin:0 0 18px;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;column-gap:14px;row-gap:0}
.is .ibfeat li{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:13px;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.3;
  padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.is .ibfeat .fi{flex:none;width:22px;height:22px;border:1.5px solid #B9D4EA;border-radius:6px;
  display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--blue)}
.is .ibfeat .fi svg{width:13px;height:13px}
@container (min-width:360px){.is .ibfeat{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.is .ibfeat li{font-size:12.5px;padding:7px 0;align-items:flex-start}.is .ibfeat .fi{margin-top:-1px}}
.is .ibcta{margin-top:auto;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:12px 16px;border-radius:10px;
  background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--blue),#1F6FB8);color:#fff;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.005em}
.is .ibcta .i{width:17px;height:17px;flex:none}
.is .ibcta .i:last-child{margin-left:auto;transition:transform .35s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
.is .ibcard:hover .ibcta .i:last-child{transform:translateX(4px)}
/* tighter vertical rhythm: less scrolling, same blocks */
.is .sec{padding:clamp(46px,5.6vw,84px) 0}
.is .ibsec{padding-bottom:clamp(24px,2.6vw,40px)}
.is .ibsec .head{max-width:880px}
.is .ibsec .head .lede{max-width:70ch}
.is .ibsec .head .lede+.lede{margin-top:14px}
.is #who{padding-top:clamp(22px,2.4vw,34px)!important;padding-bottom:clamp(40px,4.4vw,64px)}
/* #problem: two cards per row (user, 2026-08-28: "keep 2 blocks in one row, this way we save
   scroll space"). Drawing on top, copy below, both wider than the old four-high pile. No
   hover scale: it pushed the drawing's callouts past the card edge. Hover replays the
   drawing's own build-up instead (JS below re-adds .in). */
.is .pstack{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px;max-width:none;padding:0}
.is .dcard{position:static;top:auto;transform:none;display:block;min-height:0}
.is .dcard .art{aspect-ratio:640/336;height:auto;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);border-right:0;overflow:hidden;background:#F4F9FD}
.is .dcard .art svg{display:block;width:100%;height:100%}
.is .dcard.rp .pvis *{transition:none!important}
.is .dcard .tx{text-align:left;padding:24px 28px 28px;max-width:none;margin:0}
.is .dcard h3{font-size:clamp(21px,1.8vw,26px);margin:8px 0 10px}
.is .dcard p{font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.6;max-width:52ch}
.is #problem .head{margin-bottom:clamp(20px,2.4vw,30px)}
/* roles: the pill is now a link; same look */
.is .tcard a.pill{color:var(--blue);text-decoration:none}
/* back to top */
.is-totop{position:fixed;right:22px;bottom:24px;z-index:900;width:46px;height:46px;min-width:0;min-height:0;
  padding:0;margin:0;line-height:0;box-sizing:border-box;font-size:0;border-radius:50%;
  border:1px solid #EAEAEA;background:#fff;color:#0083C8;cursor:pointer;display:grid;place-items:center;
  box-shadow:0 18px 40px -18px rgba(0,40,70,.45);opacity:0;visibility:hidden;transform:translateY(12px);
  transition:opacity .3s,transform .3s,visibility .3s,background-color .2s,color .2s}
.is-totop svg{display:block;width:18px;height:18px;margin:0}
.is-totop.on{opacity:1;visibility:visible;transform:none}
.is-totop:hover{background:#0083C8;color:#fff}
body.cookies-not-set .is-totop{bottom:96px}

/* ---- narrow screens ----------------------------------------------------------- */
@media (max-width:1100px){
  /* below the two-column card there is nothing worth pinning; ordinary stacked list */
  .is .stx-card{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .is .stx-ghost{font-size:110px;top:-12px}
  .is .stx-copy{padding:30px 24px}
}
@media (max-width:1024px){
  /* the tablet/phone header overlays the page and is 64px tall */
  .is .hero{padding-top:96px}
}
@media (max-width:900px){
  .is .ibrow{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
  .is .ibcard h3{min-height:0}
  .is .ibcard:last-child{grid-column:1/-1;max-width:calc(50% - 6px)}
}
@media (max-width:820px){
  .is .nums div:nth-child(5){grid-column:span 2;border-right:0}
  .is .nums div:nth-child(5) span{max-width:none}
}
@media (max-width:640px){
  .is .ibrow{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .is .ibcard:last-child{max-width:none}
  .is .ibbody{padding:36px 18px 18px}
  .is .ibbadge{left:18px}
  .is .pstack{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}
  .is .dcard .tx{padding:20px 20px 22px}
  .is .dcard h3{font-size:21px}
  .is .dcard p{font-size:16px}
  .is-totop{right:14px;bottom:16px;width:42px;height:42px}
  body.cookies-not-set .is-totop{bottom:150px}
  .is .stx-pill{padding:7px 13px 7px 7px;font-size:13px}
  .is .stx-pill i{width:26px;height:26px}
  /* the pill rail scrolls sideways on a phone: show the scroll line under it and fade the
     right edge so the cut-off pill reads as "more this way" (user, 2026-08-28) */
  .is .stx-rail{justify-content:flex-start}
  .is .stx-pills{position:relative}
  .is .stx-rail::after{content:"";position:absolute;right:0;top:0;height:48px;width:44px;pointer-events:none;border-radius:0 100px 100px 0;
    background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(250,250,250,0),rgba(250,250,250,.92))}
  /* "Customer-Integrated" is one 19-character word: 34px overflows a 390px screen */
  .is .hero h1{font-size:clamp(26px,7.4vw,34px)}
  .is .stx-chip{display:none}
  .is .stx-dkrow{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .is .stx-tk{grid-template-columns:1.5fr 1fr 1fr}
  .is .stx-tk>span:last-child{display:none}
  .is .stx-vis{padding:14px}
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .is .ticker ul{animation:run 80s linear infinite}
  .is .stx-panel.in{animation:none}
  .is .ibcard,.is .ibfig img{transition:none}
}
</style>
<button class="is-totop" type="button" aria-label="Back to top"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 19V5"/><path d="m5 12 7-7 7 7"/></svg></button>
<script>
/* dashboards: pill rail + one card at a time, switched in place on hover or click */
(function () {
  var stax = document.querySelector('.stx-panels');
  if (!stax) return;
  var panels = [].slice.call(stax.querySelectorAll('.stx-panel'));
  var pills = [].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.stx-pill'));
  /* the screens sit in panels that are visibility:hidden until their stage is picked, and a
     lazy image inside a hidden element is never fetched - so the first switch to a stage sat
     on an empty gradient while ~90KB came down. Flip them to eager once the section is in
     range and every switch paints something that is already there. */
  function warmShots() {
    [].forEach.call(stax.querySelectorAll('.stx-shot img'), function (im) { im.loading = 'eager'; });
  }
  if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
    var wio = new IntersectionObserver(function (es) {
      if (es.some(function (e) { return e.isIntersecting; })) { wio.disconnect(); warmShots(); }
    }, { rootMargin: '1600px 0px' });
    wio.observe(stax);
  }
  /* and unconditionally once the page itself is done, so a reader who never scrolls near the
     section before clicking a jump link still gets the screens. warmShots is idempotent and
     runs after load, so it takes nothing away from the first paint. */
  addEventListener('load', function () {
    if (window.requestIdleCallback) requestIdleCallback(warmShots, { timeout: 2500 });
    else setTimeout(warmShots, 1200);
  });
  /* phone: the pill rail scrolls sideways - draw its own scroll line, because overlay
     scrollbars hide the native one and nobody knew the other pills were there */
  var railEl = document.querySelector('.stx-pills'), sbEl = document.querySelector('.stx-sb');
  if (railEl && sbEl) {
    var sbThumb = sbEl.firstElementChild;
    function sbDraw() {
      var over = railEl.scrollWidth - railEl.clientWidth;
      sbEl.classList.toggle('on', over > 4);
      if (over <= 4) return;
      var w = railEl.clientWidth / railEl.scrollWidth;
      sbThumb.style.width = (w * 100).toFixed(1) + '%';
      sbThumb.style.left = ((railEl.scrollLeft / over) * (1 - w) * 100).toFixed(1) + '%';
    }
    railEl.addEventListener('scroll', sbDraw, { passive: true });
    addEventListener('resize', sbDraw);
    sbDraw();
  }
  var reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  /* challenge cards: hovering replays the drawing's build-up (the .in class drives it) */
  if (matchMedia('(hover:hover)').matches && !reduce) {
    [].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.dcard')).forEach(function (c) {
      c.addEventListener('mouseenter', function () {
        if (!c.classList.contains('in')) return;
        c.classList.add('rp'); c.classList.remove('in'); void c.offsetWidth;
        c.classList.remove('rp'); void c.offsetWidth; c.classList.add('in');
      });
    });
  }
  /* in-place switcher (user, 2026-08-28: "instead of scroll lets just make it change or
     appear from center fast on hover plus tab clicks"). One card shown at a time, the new one
     scales up from the centre in .28s. Hover under (hover:hover), click everywhere. */
  var cur = -1;
  function goStage(i, scrollTo) {
    if (!panels[i] || i === cur) return;
    cur = i;
    pills.forEach(function (p, j) { p.classList.toggle('on', j === i); });
    panels.forEach(function (p, j) {
      var on = j === i;
      p.classList.toggle('on', on);
      if (on) {
        p.classList.remove('in'); void p.offsetWidth; p.classList.add('in');
        /* the card's own reveal targets (the console draws its gauges on .in): a hidden
           panel may never have crossed the reveal observer, so mark them now */
        [].forEach.call(p.querySelectorAll('.rv'), function (r) { r.classList.add('in'); });
      }
    });
    if (scrollTo) {
      var rail = document.querySelector('.stx-rail');
      var y = rail.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY - 96;
      window.scrollTo({ top: Math.max(0, y), behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
    }
  }
  /* hover needs intent (user, 2026-09-03). The pills sit shoulder to shoulder, so moving
     from OEE to a pill further along drags the pointer across every pill in between and each
     one fired a switch: three panels animating in within ~50ms, which reads as the section
     hanging on the old screen and then jumping. Only the pill you stop on wins now; clicks
     still switch at once. */
  var hoverT = null;
  function cancelHover() { if (hoverT) { clearTimeout(hoverT); hoverT = null; } }
  var canHover = matchMedia('(hover:hover)').matches;
  pills.forEach(function (pill, i) {
    pill.addEventListener('click', function () { cancelHover(); goStage(i); });
    if (!canHover) return;
    pill.addEventListener('mouseenter', function () {
      cancelHover();
      hoverT = setTimeout(function () { hoverT = null; goStage(i); }, 120);
    });
    pill.addEventListener('mouseleave', cancelHover);
  });
  [].forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('a[data-stage]'), function (a) {
    a.addEventListener('click', function (ev) {
      ev.preventDefault();
      goStage(parseInt(a.getAttribute('data-stage'), 10) || 0, true);
    });
  });
  goStage(0);
})();
/* back to top: shows after one screen of scrolling */
(function () {
  var b = document.querySelector('.is-totop');
  if (!b) return;
  var reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  function chk() { b.classList.toggle('on', window.scrollY > innerHeight * 0.9); }
  b.addEventListener('click', function () {
    window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
  });
  addEventListener('scroll', chk, { passive: true });
  chk();
})();
</script>
<!-- /ithena-iserv-restructure -->

<!-- ithena-hero-pad -->
<style>.is .hero{padding-top:calc(clamp(110px,8vw,122px) + 56px)}@media (max-width:1024px){.is .hero{padding-top:120px}}</style>
<!-- /ithena-hero-pad -->